			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement Tauri command handlers for text model lifecycle and file I/O\n\nIntroduce a comprehensive suite of Wind IPC service handlers under `Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers/Model/` to bridge the Mountain backend with the editor's document registry and filesystem operations. These handlers fulfill the contract required by Wind's text model service to manage the full lifecycle of open files.\n\nThe implementation covers the core CRUD operations for in-memory document models and raw file access:\n- **Model Lifecycle:** `ModelOpen` reads content from disk, infers language ID from extensions, and registers a `DocumentStateDTO` in `ApplicationState.Feature.Documents` with correct EOL handling. `ModelClose` removes entries idempotently.\n- **Model State:** `ModelGet` and `ModelGetAll` return snapshots of open documents (content, version, language ID) for UI restoration and cache hydration. `ModelUpdateContent` applies edits, increments version numbers, and marks documents as dirty.\n- **File I/O:** `TextfileRead` and `TextfileWrite` provide direct verbatim file access for tooling and resolvers without polluting the document registry. `TextfileSave` acts as a save-intent hint to clear dirty markers and log traces.\n\nAll handlers adhere to PascalCase naming, strict error handling, and the project's modular architecture, ensuring the native backend can reliably synchronize state with the Wind/Sky frontend.",
			"SHA": "4f13441eff41ba8384cc274c2eca1a8d0377bac7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
